{
  "about": "Question taken back (relay-api.md 'Question taken back'). valid / invalid: texts that pass / fail message.schema.json. body.text is REQUIRED and is exactly 'Taken back: <reason>' (reason 1-200 chars, one line, no control or bidi characters); the body is only {text, taken_back:{reason}}. questions: what the relay already holds in every relay test (id, sender, question_id, ticket, key; kind plain|review|proposal). relay: what the relay answers (expect = HTTP status; 200 = identical duplicate; error = the error code when given) given state: answered = question message ids a phone answered, taken_back = taken_back messages already stored. ws_pilatus001 is the sender, ws_other00001 another workspace, m_tt00000000000001 a plain text of the sender. Entries with `call` POST /v1/phone/answer are replayed as that phone request, entries with `request` and stored_body_lacks as POST /v1/phone/send. cases: what the workspace sends after `orch ask <ticket> --take-back` (asked_on_phones = it sent that question to phones, relay_on = the relay add-on is on, changed = the take-back changed the ticket, reason_in = what the ticket holds, send = the body or null, to/reply_to routing). inbound: messages that arrive over the relay and must NEVER take a question back (the ticket stays as is). late: answers that reach the workspace after the take-back. phone: the cards a phone shows after the events. A relay implementation replays every relay entry against the relay itself. open_questions: the questions a paired phone lists (and open_questions counts) for the workspace in the given state.",
